    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TDvuJ2KygqHcBPtkDgePBK)_\n\nStep 3 of 5 of [`devonthink-emacs-integration.org`](emacs-modular/.config/emacs-modular/docs/architecture/devonthink-emacs-integration.org). **Base: `415-devonthink-browse-tags` (#415)**, which is stacked on #414. Merge in order #414, #415, #416.\n\n## What\n- `sp-devonthink-search` (`C-c k d f`): one front end over two engines.\n  - DEVONthink search by default: the query goes to DEVONthink as typed, so `name:`, `kind:`, `tags:`, quotes, `AND`/`OR`/`NOT` work. It lists the first 50 hits (`sp-devonthink-search-limit`) with kind and page count.\n  - `C-u` asks for the engine: `devonthink`, `litdb: meaning`, `litdb: words`, `litdb: both` (the last three run the existing `sp-litdb-search` with that mode).\n- Hits have the same completion category as the browser, so all browser Embark actions work on them (open, PDF, litnote, link, tags), plus:\n  - `s` similar records (DEVONthink's \"see also\", `compare`);\n  - `v` preview of the first 3000 characters of the text (cut inside DEVONthink).\n- `sp-devonthink-similar-to-note` (`C-c k d a`): similar records for the record of the current litnote.\n- The browser's record parser now accepts two optional extra fields (kind, pages). Literate doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-devonthink-search.org`; README table row added.\n- The concordance is not in the scripting dictionary, so it is not offered (as in the design); open the record in DEVONthink for it.\n\n## Testing steps (on the Mac, fish, `~/.config/emacs-modular`)\n1. Check out the branch (`cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 416-devonthink-search; git checkout 416-devonthink-search`), restart Emacs.\n2. Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; for f in browse search; do emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/academic -l ert -l tests/sp-devonthink-$f-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit; done` → 6 and 7 tests pass.\n3. DEVONthink open on `literature`. `C-c k d f`, type a word you know occurs (e.g. `Therborn`), `RET`-less: the hits list appears in DEVONthink's rank order, each with e.g. `PDF Document, 212 pages`. Time it (the design measured about 0.5 s for 1,455 hits). Choose a hit → it opens in DEVONthink.\n4. Operators: `C-c k d f`, query `\"value form\" kind:pdf` → only PDFs with the phrase. Query `name:okane` → records by file name.\n5. Embark on a hit (`C-.`): `v` shows a `*devonthink preview*` buffer with the start of the text; `n` goes to its litnote; `t` tags it (see #415).\n6. Similar records: on a hit press `s` → a new list \"Similar to KEY.pdf:\" of related records; choose one to open. In a litnote with a `#+devonthink:` keyword (or a citekey), `C-c k d a` does the same.\n7. litdb: `C-u C-c k d f` → choose `litdb: meaning` and a query such as `exchange abstraction`. Expect the same results as `C-c k l` (`sp-litdb-search`) with the vector mode: page hits with scores; choosing one opens DEVONthink at that page. (This needs the litdb index: `C-c k I` if you never ran it.) Also try `litdb: words` and `litdb: both`.\n8. Empty search: query `zzzzzzqq` → \"No records found\" and nothing else happens.\n\n## Not tested\n- AppleScript, **not run**: `page count of`, `kind of`, `location of` on a search result; `compare record … to database …`; `plain text of` plus `text 1 thru N of` on a large record. If one fails, copy the `osascript` error: the scripts are the constants in `sp-devonthink-search.org`.\n- 7 ERT tests (Emacs 29.3) cover query quoting, parsing, annotations, rank order, opening the chosen hit, litdb mode hand-off, script text and the preview buffer. Tangle check passes.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC)_",
